    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "MED PACIPIG JAN.31,1933.\nJ.S. ELLIOT\nJ.O.WILLSON\nWATSON\nTHE THREE MUSKETERS OR RAOKSTERRSOP\nBLL STRESS.\nThe so delled\n\"Pacifie\" is too damned rough to write long hand and then\nboetde thet conelderation, I need praettee on thie dozone The purpose of this Joint\nand sevezal letter is to tell you ell and each how sorry I am that 16 was not possibbe\nfor neto see you before leaving New York and eny \"goodbye\". I had counted on doing\nso up unti)\nthe last moment when I had to make a wild dash for the train.\nYou have probably long sinee learned from Harry Knight that I have joined\nBIt in thet fast depleting class nom as the implored. There have been times on this\ntempostous voyage that I have regrebted that move. He ren Into thiek weather outside\nVietorla and 1t has been gotting worse right along. There are only twenty three firet\nclass passengers liated and todate I haven't seen more than three or four around. I\nhave visited the dining salon regularily probably urged by the same consideration\nthat prompts any one of you to cut a lunchem date at the trots\" in favor of a free\nLunch. My Seotah blood refuses to pass up food when it 1s on the house so to spe al.\nI am eating myself out of shape but figure with shirley that thaze vi11 he plenty of\ntime for dieting later on.\nPlease give my very beat to Hear Street and all the othar worthies of\nthe sub-india House. See thet Herzy's behavior stays on the same high etandard at-\ntained under ny guidanee and when you get around to it please raise the rates of\nChinese exchange so I can sell a fer Perris Wheele in the Ordent.\nMy very best also to Jenst and sydney, and again excuse me for running\namy without adlets to those who mde my long stay in New Tort much moze pleasant\nthan it would have been without then.\nSincereky\nBix"
